1538 0 obj
<<
  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 1537 0 R
  /Alt (This conceptual diagram illustrates the Copernicus Land Monitoring Service (CLMS) rule for mapping land cover changes, specifically how the Minimum Mapping Unit (MMU) of 0.5 ha is applied in relation to Natura 2000 (N2K) polygons. The diagram presents four panels: 1. **Image t0:** Displays an initial land cover state with a large area classified as 1.1.1 (red) and a horizontal strip classified as 1.2.1 (grey). 2. **Image t+1:** Shows a later land cover state where the 1.2.1 area has transformed into a vertical strip, indicating a land cover change. A segment within this new vertical 1.2.1 strip is highlighted with a dashed outline and labelled '< 0,5 ha', signifying a change area smaller than the standard 0.5 ha MMU. 3. **N2K t0:** Represents the initial state of a Natura 2000 (N2K) polygon, mirroring 'Image t0,' with the horizontal 1.2.1 strip outlined in black to denote it as an existing N2K site. 4. **N2K t+1:** Illustrates the final mapped land cover for N2K areas after the change. The entire new vertical 1.2.1 strip, critically including the portion previously labelled '< 0,5 ha', is mapped as a continuous 1.2.1 area. This demonstrates the rule that even land cover changes smaller than the 0.5 ha Minimum Mapping Unit are mapped if they are connected to an existing CLMS Natura 2000 polygon. The original horizontal 1.2.1 area from N2K t0 is also depicted as being integrated into the new, transformed configuration, or fragmented by the change.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
  >>]
  /K [3]
  /Pg 3796 0 R
>>
endobj

