1545 0 obj
<<
  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 1544 0 R
  /Alt (Conceptual diagram illustrating the Copernicus Land Monitoring Service (CLMS) change mapping rules, specifically for an urban site's expansion and its implications for Natura 2000 (N2K) polygons between a reference year t0 and a later reference year t+1. The diagram shows four panels: 1. **Image t0:** Displays a land cover classified as 1.1.1 (representing urban areas, from context). A brown area of change, labelled '< 0.5 ha', is present at the bottom. 2. **Image t+1:** Shows the same land cover, 1.1.1, but the brown area has expanded to '> 0.5 ha' in the center of the panel. This represents the enlargement of an urban site. 3. **N2K t0:** Illustrates the Natura 2000 mapping at t0. The entire area is classified as 1.1.1, and the initial change polygon (< 0.5 ha) is not mapped as an N2K feature. 4. **N2K t+1:** Illustrates the Natura 2000 mapping at t+1. The background remains 1.1.1. The expanded brown area (> 0.5 ha) is now mapped as a new N2K polygon, outlined in black, and classified as 1.3.1 (a new land cover class within the N2K context), split into two sections. This demonstrates that changes greater than 0.5 hectares connected to an existing CLMS Natura 2000 polygon are always mapped.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
  >>]
  /K [15]
  /Pg 3794 0 R
>>
endobj

