1552 0 obj
<<
  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 1551 0 R
  /Alt (This diagram illustrates the process of mapping land cover changes, specifically urban expansion, within Copernicus Land Monitoring Service (CLMS) Natura 2000 (N2K) polygons between two reference years, t0 and t+1. The diagram consists of four panels: 1. **Image t0**: Shows an initial land cover state with three classes: 1.1.1 (Urban fabric, red), 2.1.1 (Arable land, light yellow), and 4.1 (Forests and semi-natural areas, yellow). 2. **Image t+1**: Shows the same area at a later reference year, revealing changes. The existing 1.1.1 (Urban fabric) area has expanded. Two new areas are demarcated with dashed borders: one area of 0.1 ha, originally 4.1, converted to 1.1.1; and another area of 0.4 ha, originally 2.1.1, converted to 1.1.1. 3. **N2K t0**: Represents the Natura 2000 mapping at reference year t0, which is identical to the land cover composition shown in Image t0. 4. **N2K t+1**: Shows the updated Natura 2000 mapping at reference year t+1. The changes observed in Image t+1 are incorporated. The original 1.1.1 area remains, and the two newly converted polygons (0.1 ha and 0.4 ha), totaling 0.5 ha of urban expansion, are now mapped as 1.1.1 polygons within the N2K product. The surrounding text indicates that 'changes > 0.5 ha connected to an existing CLMS N2K polygon are always mapped,' and that the example specifically shows an 'enlargement by more than 0.5ha'.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
  >>]
  /K [8]
  /Pg 3794 0 R
>>
endobj

