  /Alt (This diagram illustrates the rule for mapping land cover changes within Copernicus Land Monitoring Service (CLMS) Natura 2000 (N2K) polygons, specifically when changes are greater than 0.5 hectares and connected to an existing N2K polygon. The diagram consists of four panels comparing two time points (t0 and t+1) and two data interpretations (Image and N2K): 1. **Image t0:** Shows an initial state with a red rectangular area labeled '1.1.1' (likely 'Continuous urban fabric' based on context) embedded within a larger yellow area labeled '4.1'. 2. **Image t+1:** Shows an expansion of the '1.1.1' area from t0. The original rectangle has extended into an L-shape. A new, horizontally adjacent rectangular segment of this expansion is outlined with a dashed line and explicitly labeled '> 0.5 ha'. 3. **N2K t0:** Represents the Natura 2000 polygon corresponding to the 'Image t0' state, showing the same single rectangular '1.1.1' area. 4. **N2K t+1:** Represents the updated Natura 2000 polygon after applying the change mapping rule. The entire L-shaped expanded area from 'Image t+1' is now mapped as a single contiguous '1.1.1' polygon. This illustrates that because the change (expansion) exceeds 0.5 hectares and is connected to an existing N2K polygon, the entire new extent of the land cover class is mapped.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
  >>]
  /K [0]
