3194 0 obj
<<
  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 3193 0 R
  /Alt (This pie chart illustrates the distribution of total observed land cover change processes across Europe for the combined periods 2006-2012 and 2012-2018. The chart displays 18 distinct change categories, each with its percentage share of the total changes. The largest shares are: * Agricultural intensification: 16% * Tree encroachment: 16% * Agricultural conversion to cropland: 14% * Urbanization: 13% * Expansion of grassland: 9% * Intensification of grassland use: 7% * De-urbanization: 4% * Agricultural conversion to managed grassland: 4% * Forest increase - Natural succession: 3% * Woody plant encroachment: 3% * Scrub encroachment: 2% * Grassland degradation: 2% * Extensification of grassland use: 2% Smaller categories, each representing 1% of the total change, include: * Agricultural extensification * Occupation by water infrastructures / Hydrological restructuring * Drainage * Hydrological restoration * Other The chart highlights that agricultural changes (intensification, conversion to cropland, extensification, conversion to managed grassland) account for a significant portion of the total land cover dynamics. Tree and woody plant encroachment, along with forest increase, also represent substantial shares. Urbanization and de-urbanization processes demonstrate dynamic land use changes.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
  >>]
  /K [0]
  /Pg 3726 0 R
>>
endobj

