3198 0 obj
<<
  /Type /StructElem
  /S /Figure
  /P 3197 0 R
  /Alt (A combined table and grouped bar chart illustrating the area coverage in hectares (HA) for eight Level 1 land cover classes and 'No Data' within Natura 2000 (N2K) sites and their buffer zones (N2K AoI) for the reference years 2006, 2012, and 2018, along with absolute and percentage changes between the periods 2006-2012 and 2012-2018. The Level 1 classes and their corresponding numeric codes and colours are: - Class 1: Urban (red) - Class 2: Cropland (light yellow) - Class 3: Woodland and forest (dark green) - Class 4: Grassland (yellow-green) - Class 5: Heathland and scrub (light green) - Class 6: Open spaces with little or no vegetation (light grey-green) - Class 7: Wetland (light purple) - Class 8: Water (light blue) - Class 0: No Data (white) The area coverage for each class is: - **2006:** - Urban: 2,815,009 HA - Cropland: 15,415,698 HA - Woodland and forest: 24,665,098 HA - Grassland: 11,270,402 HA - Heathland and scrub: 4,689,384 HA - Open spaces with little or no vegetation: 1,795,959 HA - Wetland: 735,350 HA - Water: 1,792,739 HA - No Data: 2,457 HA - **2012:** - Urban: 2,889,208 HA - Cropland: 15,393,883 HA - Woodland and forest: 24,683,118 HA - Grassland: 11,207,789 HA - Heathland and scrub: 4,656,799 HA - Open spaces with little or no vegetation: 1,816,606 HA - Wetland: 730,511 HA - Water: 1,804,084 HA - No Data: 97 HA - **2018:** - Urban: 2,940,737 HA - Cropland: 15,430,349 HA - Woodland and forest: 24,698,560 HA - Grassland: 11,121,261 HA - Heathland and scrub: 4,643,509 HA - Open spaces with little or no vegetation: 1,808,837 HA - Wetland: 728,157 HA - Water: 1,810,686 HA - No Data: 0 HA Changes in area coverage: - **Change 2006-2012:** - Urban: +74,199 HA (+2.64%) - Cropland: -22,815 HA (-0.14%) - Woodland and forest: +18,020 HA (+0.07%) - Grassland: -62,613 HA (-0.56%) - Heathland and scrub: -32,584 HA (-0.69%) - Open spaces with little or no vegetation: +20,647 HA (+1.15%) - Wetland: -4,839 HA (-0.66%) - Water: +11,346 HA (+0.63%) - No Data: -2,360 HA (-96.04%) - **Change 2012-2018:** - Urban: +51,529 HA (+1.78%) - Cropland: +36,466 HA (+0.24%) - Woodland and forest: +15,442 HA (+0.06%) - Grassland: -86,528 HA (-0.77%) - Heathland and scrub: -13,290 HA (-0.29%) - Open spaces with little or no vegetation: -7,769 HA (-0.43%) - Wetland: -2,354 HA (-0.32%) - Water: +6,602 HA (+0.37%) - No Data: -97 HA (-100.00%) Overall, 'Woodland and forest' consistently holds the highest area, followed by 'Cropland' and 'Grassland', with 'Wetland' and 'Water' being the rarest classes. 'Urban' areas showed continuous growth across both periods, gaining 74,199 HA (2006-2012) and 51,529 HA (2012-2018). 'Grassland' experienced the most significant losses, totaling -62,613 HA (2006-2012) and -86,528 HA (2012-2018). 'No Data' area decreased dramatically, reaching zero by 2018, indicating improved data completeness.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
  >>]
  /K [0]
  /Pg 3724 0 R
>>
endobj

